ANACREON 10
"Das Rhinegeld"
0    ; Random Scenario
1 8  ; 1 to 8 players
39   ; 39x39 galaxy
164  ; Number of planets
1    ; Intermediate
75 0 ; 75+ years
4021 ; Start Year
BEGINTEXT

                 *** Das Rhinegeld - The Ring Saga ***
                An intermediate scenario for 1-8 players.


                            --Developed  by--

                            Michael O'Connell
                         James "Blue" Carstensen
                               Edziu Iskra
                            William Barlettano
                              Derek Habermas


Special thanks to Shannon Dwyer, Craig Garrettson, Greg Belmonte,
and Wagner (for his music).

NEWPAGE

                               _DAS RHINEGELD_
                                The Ring Saga

Background:
     The Terran Empire once stretched halfway across the Orion arm of the
galaxy, spreading outward from Earth into the sparse regions of the Belt.
Historians may dispute the actual details, but most agree that if Sol had
not unexpectedly gone nova in 3012, humankind could have eventually
colonized the entire galaxy.
     As it were, with the collapse of the Inner Sphere communications
nexus, most of the Imperial regions fell into isolated autonomy.  Indeed,
the eight Citizen-Govenors on the frontier at first had their hands full
maintaining control, and paid no attention to the once-thriving center.

     Until 4018, when reports began to filter through the Rim that Earth
had actually survived the catyclysm, and was not destroyed, but merely
hidden in the center, in the nova's remnants...

NEWPAGE

     If the Emerald Throne was still intact, all it needed was someone to
claim it... and all of the Govenors were heirs.
     The first one to reach the center, and claim Earth as their own,
would be the new Emperor, with the galaxy at their command.

     It would not be simple.  Having at most three planets under their
control, none of the Govenors had the necessary industrial base.  Each
still had control of 1/8th of the minefields they had maintained as part
of the Empire's defenses, but only had knowledge of the locations they
controlled.  And none of the Govenors had the level of technology that the
old Empire boasted, having to painstakingly rebuild the knowledge.
     But to the one who gained the center first, power and riches beyond
their imaginings.  Those who lost were doomed to a return to servitude.

     The race was on.
     
NEWPAGE
ENDTEXT

